What the fork adds
------------------

This fork exists to be an instance we host, and a URL our clients can point at
instead of somebody else's deployment — not to rewrite the extraction. On top of
upstream it adds:

  * a declared public contract. The OpenAPI document's `info.version` is the
    contract version (which a client compares against what it supports) and
    `x-mg-contract` names the capabilities, the data categories and the runtime
    facts. `GET /schema.json` serves the same facts flat, from the same
    `openapi.yaml`, so the document and the route cannot disagree, and a test
    fails if a documented path is not mounted or a capability is claimed without
    a path behind it.
  * `GET /data/version` — the path mg.js already asks for and upstream answers
    404 — reporting the game version the served data and sprites were built
    from, without a fresh fetch of the game's version endpoint.
  * this NOTICE, and the matching README section.

The bundle extraction, the platform-API polling, the sprite/atlas/Rive export,
the weather station and the history recorder are upstream's work. They are
unchanged here except where a commit in this repository says otherwise.
